Given case A there's another pair that fits the same pattern:
Get Greyswandir or Frost Bane, ditch Magicbane.

Setting aside the fact that I don't subscribe to that school of
thought it's a valid approach.  Wield the best possible melee
weapon whether you're a spell caster or melee fighter.  The
reason I don't subscribe to that school is MB has enough other
uses that I wouldn't ditch it.

Given enough choices, I'd dual wield Grey/FB with a silver
saber or long sword and keep MB ready to wield when it's
strengths are needed.  Plus the usual quiver of elven daggers,
wands, spells and so on.

Another problem is they aren't in the same item categories
so calling them a pair makes less sense.  Plain sack and
oilskin sack are both container tools.  Sting and Magicbane
are both dagger skill classes.  MB and Frosty are both
weapons but different skill class.  That's too much like
saying a stethoscope and a frost horn form a pair for my
tastes.



